{%- comment -%}
  Designer/label detection. Vendor is not a reliable field on this catalogue
  (everything is set to the shop name), so external designers are parsed
  from the product title, matching the known list used across the site nav.

  "Little Bo Peep" is the in-house signature collection — it is NOT a
  catch-all for "title didn't match a known designer". An earlier version of
  this snippet used that as a fallback and it wrongly labelled ~74% of the
  catalogue (488 of 655 products) as Little Bo Peep, since most products
  simply don't name a designer in the title at all. That made "Shop the
  Little Bo Peep Collection" show almost the entire store.

  There is currently no real Shopify field (tag, vendor, type) marking which
  products are genuinely the in-house line — confirmed by querying the
  catalogue directly. Until the merchant tags their real Little Bo Peep
  products (tag: "Little Bo Peep"), this correctly returns blank for
  anything unmatched rather than guessing. Once that tag exists, every
  Little Bo Peep link/section on the site starts working with no further
  code changes.
  Usage: {% capture brand %}{% render 'brand-of', product: product %}{% endcapture %}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if product.tags contains 'Little Bo Peep' -%}Little Bo Peep
{%- elsif product.title contains 'Ceaser Blanco' -%}Ceaser Blanco
{%- elsif product.title contains 'Ela Confection' -%}Ela Confection
{%- elsif product.title contains 'Lapin House' -%}Lapin House
{%- elsif product.title contains 'Balloon Chic' -%}Balloon Chic
{%- elsif product.title contains 'Abuela Tata' -%}Abuela Tata
{%- elsif product.title contains 'Mitch & Son' -%}Mitch & Son
{%- elsif product.title contains 'Little A' -%}Little A
{%- elsif product.title contains 'Deolinda' -%}Deolinda
{%- elsif product.title contains 'Babyfer' -%}Babyfer
{%- elsif product.title contains 'Monnalisa' -%}Monnalisa
{%- elsif product.title contains 'Sonata' -%}Sonata
